---
import ServicePage from '../components/ServicePage.astro';
---

<ServicePage
  title="Lifestyle Medicine"
  description="Evidence-based lifestyle medicine telehealth in Florida. Chronic disease prevention and management through nutrition, sleep, stress, and movement guidance."
  eyebrow="lifestyle medicine"
  heroTitle="Most chronic disease is preventable. And reversible."
  heroSub="Lifestyle medicine uses evidence-based interventions in nutrition, sleep, activity, and stress management to prevent and often reverse chronic disease. We help you apply them."
  chipLabel="preventive care"
  chipClass="chip-sage"
  heroSurface="rgba(168,184,155,0.2)"
  heroImage="/images/hero-lifestyle-medicine.jpg"
  values={[
    {
      icon: "○",
      heading: "Nutrition guidance",
      body: "Evidence-based dietary approaches tailored to your health goals: blood sugar control, weight management, cardiovascular health, and energy."
    },
    {
      icon: "▲",
      heading: "Sleep as medicine",
      body: "Poor sleep drives inflammation, insulin resistance, weight gain, and mood disorders. Improving sleep quality is one of the highest-leverage health interventions."
    },
    {
      icon: "⬡",
      heading: "Stress and chronic disease",
      body: "Chronic stress is a direct driver of cardiovascular disease, metabolic dysfunction, and immune suppression. We help you manage it with real strategies."
    }
  ]}
  features={[
    {
      heading: "Type 2 diabetes is often reversible with the right approach",
      body: "Type 2 diabetes and prediabetes are driven primarily by insulin resistance, which is a lifestyle-modifiable condition. Dietary changes, targeted activity, sleep optimization, and in some cases medication can put many patients into remission. We use this evidence-based framework alongside your medical management to give you the best possible outcomes.",
      chipLabel: "metabolic health",
      chipClass: "chip-sage",
      imgAlt: "Colorful vegetables on a plate",
      image: "/images/feat-lifestyle-1.jpg"
    },
    {
      heading: "Cardiovascular risk starts with lifestyle",
      body: "Hypertension, high cholesterol, and cardiovascular disease are significantly influenced by diet, activity, sleep, and stress. We don't just prescribe medications. We build a real lifestyle plan that attacks risk factors at the root. Medications may still be needed, but they work better and may be reduced over time when lifestyle is addressed seriously.",
      chipLabel: "cardiovascular health",
      chipClass: "chip-coral",
      imgAlt: "Running shoes on the pavement",
      image: "/images/feat-lifestyle-2.jpg",
      flip: true
    }
  ]}
  testimonials={[
    {
      quote: "my A1C dropped from 7.8 to 5.9 in six months without changing my medications. it was the dietary and sleep changes we made together.",
      attr: "Lifestyle Medicine Patient — Bradenton, FL"
    },
    {
      quote: "i expected a pamphlet about eating vegetables. i got a real, individualized plan backed by my labs. completely different experience.",
      attr: "Lifestyle Medicine Patient — Sarasota, FL"
    },
    {
      quote: "my blood pressure medication was reduced after three months of serious lifestyle work. that was the goal and we hit it.",
      attr: "Lifestyle Medicine Patient — Tampa, FL"
    }
  ]}
  steps={[
    {
      heading: "Health and lifestyle assessment",
      body: "We review your current health conditions, medications, daily habits, sleep patterns, diet, activity level, and stress load. The full picture."
    },
    {
      heading: "Labs and baselines",
      body: "Metabolic, hormonal, and inflammatory markers give us a baseline to measure progress against. Without measurements, you can't track improvement."
    },
    {
      heading: "Individualized lifestyle plan",
      body: "A practical, realistic plan built around your actual life: what you eat, how you sleep, how you move, and how you manage stress. Followed up every 6-8 weeks."
    }
  ]}
  faq={[
    {
      q: "Is lifestyle medicine just diet advice?",
      a: "No. Lifestyle medicine is a recognized medical specialty that uses evidence-based interventions across six pillars: nutrition, physical activity, sleep, stress management, avoidance of risky substances, and social connection. It is far more comprehensive than generic diet advice."
    },
    {
      q: "Can lifestyle changes actually reverse chronic disease?",
      a: "For many patients, yes. Type 2 diabetes remission through diet is well-documented. Hypertension can often be managed or eliminated with lifestyle changes. We are honest about what the evidence supports and what it doesn't."
    },
    {
      q: "Do I still need my medications?",
      a: "Lifestyle changes work alongside medications, not always instead of them. In some cases, as your health improves, medications can be reduced or discontinued. We make those decisions carefully based on your progress."
    },
    {
      q: "How is this different from just going to the gym and eating better?",
      a: "It's personalized to your labs, health conditions, and specific risk factors. We tell you what to prioritize based on what will move the needle most for your specific situation, and we track the results."
    }
  ]}
/>
